+ * Android (msm-poweroff.c do_msm_poweroff) first sets the type to
+ * SHUTDOWN (qpnp_pon_system_pwr_off), then drops PS_HOLD; do_msm_restart
+ * sets HARD_RESET (WARM_RESET only for a dump) before every reset.
+ * The kernel does the same: the PS_HOLD reset type of the PMK8350 PON_PBS
+ * block (SID 0, 0x0800; DT pon_pbs@800 "qcom,system-reset") is set to
+ * SHUTDOWN, then PSCI SYSTEM_OFF (if it returns: SYSTEM_RESET, which also
+ * drops PS_HOLD). Before a restart a SHUTDOWN type is set to HARD_RESET.
+ * Boot-arg negronipoweroff (default 0):
+ *   0  PS_HOLD type SHUTDOWN, then SYSTEM_OFF (SYSTEM_RESET if it returns)
+ *   1  SYSTEM_OFF only (the 0211 behavior, for comparison)
